1
00:00:02,180 --> 00:00:05,100
=The Truth (Season 4)=
(Behind-the-Scenes Cast Interview)

2
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:06,390
You only have one thing to do.

3
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:07,060
(Talking with the director)
In a bit,

4
00:00:07,060 --> 00:00:08,180
when you're crouching and crying,

5
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:09,070
(Haomei got it)
look up at him.

6
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:09,830
Look at this camera.

7
00:00:11,490 --> 00:00:12,000
Let's go.

8
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:13,230
Okay, crouch down first.

9
00:00:14,840 --> 00:00:16,990
(Crouches obediently)
Try to stay emotional for a few seconds.

10
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,020
(Getting into character)
This is your state right now.

11
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:20,340
(Filming)

12
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:22,190
Are you Tui Haomei?

13
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:23,470
I'm Ke Coffee.

14
00:00:25,360 --> 00:00:26,060
Ke!

15
00:00:26,060 --> 00:00:26,640
It's me.

16
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:27,100
Is that you?

17
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:28,150
It's me.

18
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:29,340
I...

19
00:00:29,340 --> 00:00:30,660
I'm Tui Haomei!

20
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:31,900
Haomei?

21
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:32,910
Why are you here?

22
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:35,140
Are you alone?

23
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:36,560
Where's Qian?

24
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:37,550
Qian?

25
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:39,790
Where's Qian? Qian!

26
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:42,260
Qian!

27
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:43,630
Qian's fine. She's right here.

28
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:44,830
It's your first time on The Truth,

29
00:00:44,840 --> 00:00:47,150
so what was your first impression
of everyone?

30
00:00:47,160 --> 00:00:48,060
(Li Yi as Tui Haomei)
I was pretty happy.

31
00:00:48,060 --> 00:00:49,470
(Happy)
And I thought they were really nice.

32
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:54,470
They'd surprise me
during our interactions.

33
00:00:54,480 --> 00:00:56,150
Like Ke Coffee, for example.

34
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:01,780
It's okay now.

35
00:01:02,170 --> 00:01:03,550
(Softly comforting her)
Okay.

36
00:01:03,550 --> 00:01:04,269
You're not scared at all.

37
00:01:04,269 --> 00:01:05,269
You're amazing.

38
00:01:05,269 --> 00:01:06,560
You can even hold him.

39
00:01:06,620 --> 00:01:09,140
(Scared himself,
but still protecting her)

40
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:10,140
(Maximum sense of security)

41
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:11,110
Was there anyone

42
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:12,510
who was different
from what you expected?

43
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:17,550
Ding Chengxin, I guess.

44
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:18,110
I think

45
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:20,110
my part was probably pretty scary,

46
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:23,790
and he didn't really

47
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:25,710
come forward much the whole time.

48
00:01:25,720 --> 00:01:26,390
Come on.

49
00:01:27,150 --> 00:01:28,490
Ke,

50
00:01:28,520 --> 00:01:29,460
come back a little.

51
00:01:29,460 --> 00:01:30,860
(Needs just a little reassurance)

52
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:32,270
Come sit.

53
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:34,870
Oh my God!

54
00:01:34,880 --> 00:01:35,670
My legs!

55
00:01:37,360 --> 00:01:38,670
I really scared him.

56
00:01:38,760 --> 00:01:39,830
Sorry about that.

57
00:01:39,830 --> 00:01:40,680
(So sorry)
Yeah.

58
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:42,230
If you get to come back again,

59
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:43,950
what kind of role would you want to try?

60
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:46,550
(Comedy type)
I want to be the funny one.

61
00:01:47,180 --> 00:01:48,940
(The comedians taking photos)

62
00:01:56,440 --> 00:01:57,430
(Running through the scene)
You guys...

63
00:01:57,680 --> 00:01:58,310
Us?

64
00:01:58,320 --> 00:01:58,950
What about us?

65
00:01:58,960 --> 00:01:59,550
Us?

66
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:01,310
Who even are you?

67
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:01,990
I...

68
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:04,350
(Introduces himself)
I'm Liu Lian Wangfan.

69
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:05,870
(Very respectful)
Hello, boss.

70
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:07,310
(Hypothetically)
If they say that, just jump in.

71
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:08,070
Did you want to kill him?

72
00:02:08,080 --> 00:02:09,509
Just say, "Shut up".

73
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:10,500
I'll shut up.

74
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:11,480
(Message received)

75
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:12,150
You can jump right in.

76
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:12,790
If they ask,

77
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:14,070
"Were you trying to kill him"?

78
00:02:14,440 --> 00:02:15,510
Then when they stop talking,

79
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:15,870
I'll say that line.

80
00:02:15,870 --> 00:02:16,920
Right.

81
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:18,310
So you can reveal something right away?

82
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:19,870
If they want to talk to me first,

83
00:02:19,880 --> 00:02:20,510
I can talk with them?

84
00:02:20,510 --> 00:02:21,000
Right.

85
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,470
(All about improvising)
Just play off them like you did earlier.

86
00:02:22,480 --> 00:02:23,470
It's fine.

87
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:24,860
(Fully in character)

88
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:26,830
I'm Liu Lian Wangfan.

89
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:31,190
This is the key to Manager Tui's office.

90
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:34,950
You've probably never
been inside, right?

91
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:35,510
No.

92
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:36,990
He never lets outsiders in.

93
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:39,190
Take the key.

94
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:39,510
Okay.

95
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:40,830
Go see

96
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:43,150
shady stuff he's been doing in there.

97
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:44,950
(Liu Xiaoting as Liu Lian Wangfan)
Away from the crosstalk stage,

98
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:46,590
you're doing immersive acting
on a variety show.

99
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:48,070
How does it feel different?

100
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:48,670
How should I put it?

101
00:02:48,680 --> 00:02:50,070
It's a completely new experience.

102
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:52,190
(Familiar)
Crosstalk feels familiar.

103
00:02:52,360 --> 00:02:53,790
(Familiar partner)
My partner,

104
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:55,460
(Familiar audience)
the audience,

105
00:02:55,460 --> 00:02:56,880
(Familiar theater)
and the theater.

106
00:02:56,880 --> 00:02:58,790
(Unfamiliar setting)
Now I'm somewhere unfamiliar,

107
00:02:58,960 --> 00:03:00,590
(Unfamiliar people)
with people I don't know.

108
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:04,790
I still have to keep everything moving.

109
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:05,870
So,

110
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:09,390
there's a lot more going on in my head.

111
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:11,230
I'm not as relaxed
as I am doing crosstalk.

112
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:12,390
During filming,

113
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:14,870
how did it feel
acting opposite Jin Jing?

114
00:03:14,880 --> 00:03:16,550
I thought she was incredibly relaxed.

115
00:03:16,680 --> 00:03:18,150
I'm here to settle a score.

116
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:21,230
With who?

117
00:03:21,560 --> 00:03:23,070
Jin Cardashian.

118
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:24,470
You're here for me?

119
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:25,590
No way.

120
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:28,270
You haven't been home
for seven days and nights.

121
00:03:29,080 --> 00:03:31,110
I knew you'd be here.

122
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:34,350
Which home of mine

123
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:35,270
do you mean?

124
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:37,190
Compared with me,

125
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:39,670
I've done very few variety
or reality shows,

126
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:40,750
so

127
00:03:40,760 --> 00:03:44,750
I'm a little limited in what I can do.

128
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:47,430
While interacting with the players,

129
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:48,990
did anything really stick with you?

130
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:52,630
What stuck with me most was Jin Jing.

131
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:56,670
She said maybe I
could join Amazing Night 3.

132
00:03:56,670 --> 00:03:58,400
(Special invite from Jin)

133
00:03:58,400 --> 00:03:59,070
Thank you.

134
00:03:59,080 --> 00:04:01,950
If anyone
from Amazing Night 3 sees this,

135
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:03,550
let's talk.

136
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:04,590
(Applying online)
I want in too.

137
00:04:05,100 --> 00:04:06,700
(Pretty please)

138
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:09,230
When you said,
"How am I any worse“

139
00:04:09,240 --> 00:04:10,150
“than He Yiwei"?

140
00:04:10,160 --> 00:04:11,750
what were you thinking?

141
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:14,150
Who's that He-something-wei?

142
00:04:14,360 --> 00:04:15,980
He Yiwei.

143
00:04:15,980 --> 00:04:16,800
(That's me)

144
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:17,670
That's him.

145
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:18,390
That guy.

146
00:04:18,399 --> 00:04:21,060
Tell me, how am I worse than him?

147
00:04:21,779 --> 00:04:24,190
You're worse in every way!

148
00:04:24,190 --> 00:04:25,400
(That's his reputation)

149
00:04:25,870 --> 00:04:27,500
I was just making fun of myself.

150
00:04:29,230 --> 00:04:30,830
That was meant to be self-deprecating.

151
00:04:30,840 --> 00:04:33,750
Is it my looks or my height?

152
00:04:33,760 --> 00:04:34,350
What's the difference?

153
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:35,350
It's obvious.

154
00:04:35,420 --> 00:04:37,180
(Comparison steals your joy)

155
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:38,430
I don't think I'm that much worse.

156
00:04:38,430 --> 00:04:40,020
(Hurt)

157
00:04:40,200 --> 00:04:42,190
How do you see Liu Lian Wangfan
as a character?

158
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:43,630
How is he different from you?

159
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,670
He's not really a bad guy.

160
00:04:46,680 --> 00:04:48,550
Even though he had a motive to kill,

161
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:51,670
everything he did was for his sister.

162
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:55,630
She'd been through some terrible things,

163
00:04:56,160 --> 00:04:58,870
and it left her miserable and withdrawn.

164
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:01,190
From beginning to end,

165
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:02,150
he was doing it all for his sister.

166
00:05:02,160 --> 00:05:04,070
I think he's a good brother.

167
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:05,270
I wouldn't call him a bad person.

168
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:06,590
If it were me,

169
00:05:06,600 --> 00:05:08,470
the main difference

170
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:09,670
is I wouldn't be that impulsive.

171
00:05:09,960 --> 00:05:11,550
But just like him,

172
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:13,590
I'd do anything to protect my family.

173
00:05:16,540 --> 00:05:17,390
=The Truth (Season 4)=

174
00:05:17,390 --> 00:05:18,490
(SVIP updates Wed & Thu at noon)

175
00:05:18,490 --> 00:05:19,540
(VIP updates next day at noon,
one week early)
